<title>PORTUGAL: Yield falls on Portugal 5-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Portugal 5-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Portuguese Institute for Public Credit Management auction of 25 billion escudos of five-year fixed-rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>    ISSUER: Republic of Portugal   MATURITY: 23 Mar 2002</p>
<p>AMOUNT PLACED: 20.625 bln esc  COUPON: 5.75 percent</p>
<p>PAYMENT DATE: 4 June 1997</p>
<p>AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 5.786933</p>
<p>HIGHEST ACCEPTED: 5.80  LOWEST: 5.75</p>
<p>BIDS: 71.55 bln esc PAYMENT FREQUENCY: Annual</p>
<p>S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 188.53 billion escudos the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
</text>
